{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Before Moses and before Eleazar.</b> This tells that they did not stand before them except in the fortieth year, after Aaron died (ibid.)." "<b>Before Moses.</b> And afterward before Eleazar? Is it possible that if Moses did not know, Eleazar would know? Rather, emend the verse and interpret it — words of Rabbi Yoshiya. Abba Chanan in the name of Rabbi Elazar says: they were sitting in the study hall and stood before all of them (ibid.; Bava Batra 119)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:57.824976323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}